Chapter: FilesChangeCostTest
  cites Works chapter GopFiles
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 What a Files directory change costs. The Monitor is the desk's only
 heap instrument and only one pane is focused at a time, so the pane
 cannot observe itself; `alloc-bytes 0` advances the allocator by
 nothing and answers the frontier, which needs no pane at all.

 The first line is the control. A probe that reads the frontier twice
 with nothing between must answer a difference of zero; any other answer
 means the instrument allocates and every reading below is its own
 footprint (L-FALSIF).

 The third line is the claim itself. A directory change builds a fresh
 entry list and nothing reuses the previous one, so a second identical
 listing costs what the first cost. Equality there IS the accumulation
 a long session pays for, measured rather than argued, and a run where
 the second listing were free would falsify it.

 The last line is what the row could not have guessed. The cost is
 neither a constant nor a function of the entry count: measured
 2026-09-08 on this fixture, the root's two entries cost 39,984 bytes
 and a ONE entry subdirectory cost 67,376, because a subdirectory walks
 a FAT chain that the root does not. So a bound on a long Files session
 is a statement about the DEPTH and the chain, never about how many
 files a person can see.

Section: Body

  fcc-yn : Boolean -> Text
  fcc-yn (v) = if v then "PASS" else "FAIL"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let c0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let c1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("the probe allocates nothing: " & fcc-yn (c1 - c0 == 0))
      m <- gfat-mount-esp
      if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "mount FAILED"
      else act
        let a0 = alloc-bytes 0
        in act
          e1 <- gfl-list-cur (m.gm-vol) [0 - 1]
          let a1 = alloc-bytes 0
          in act
            e2 <- gfl-list-cur (m.gm-vol) [0 - 1]
            let a2 = alloc-bytes 0
            in act
              print-line-uni ("a listing allocates: " & fcc-yn (a1 - a0 > 0))
              print-line-uni ("a second listing costs the same: " & fcc-yn (a2 - a1 == a1 - a0))
              print-line-uni ("root entries: " & show (list-length e1))
              d <- gfat-resolve (m.gm-vol) "EFI"
              when d
                is None -> print-line-uni "EFI not found"
                is Just (de) -> act
                  let b0 = alloc-bytes 0
                  in act
                    e3 <- gfl-list-cur (m.gm-vol) [0 - 1, de.de-cluster]
                    let b1 = alloc-bytes 0
                    in act
                      print-line-uni ("the cost does not follow the entry count: " & fcc-yn (list-length e3 < list-length e1 & b1 - b0 > a1 - a0))
                    end
                  end
                end
              end
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
